---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Otherwise Hyperarchive — Micol Gelsi">
<article class="hyperarchive" id="top">
  <div class="hyper-top"><span>EMAP RESIDENCY PROPOSAL / ARTISTIC RESEARCH / WEB + PUBLIC SPACE</span><a href={base}>← PORTFOLIO</a></div>
  <header class="hyper-hero"><div class="hyper-hero-stars" aria-hidden="true"><span>✳</span><span>★</span><span>✳</span><span>✦</span><span>★</span><span>✳</span><span>✦</span><span>★</span><span>✳</span><span>✦</span><span>★</span><span>✳</span></div><span>OTHERWISE HYPERARCHIVE / RESEARCH ATLAS / 2027</span><h1>MAP THE<br/>SUBTRACTED<span class="hyper-accent">_</span></h1><p>INPUT: SUBTRACTED SPACE / PROCESS: COLLECTIVE ARCHIVE / OUTPUT: PUBLIC INTERFACE</p><small>CRITICAL MAPPING ★ ALLIED TECHNOLOGIES ★ COLLECTIVE MEDIA INFRASTRUCTURES</small></header>
  <nav class="hyper-nav" aria-label="Proposal sections"><a href="#concept">01 CONCEPT</a><a href="#untamed">02 PREVIOUS</a><a href="#system">03 SYSTEM</a><a href="#space">04 SPACE</a><a href="#loop">05 LOOP</a><a href="#process">06 PROCESS</a><a href="#references">07 REFERENCES</a></nav>
  <section id="concept" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">01 / RESEARCH QUESTION</span><div><h2>Detect / <em>map / reconfigure.</em></h2><p>SUBTRACTION = restricted access / erased memory / controlled visibility / lost digital autonomy. MAP = identify mechanisms, actors, boundaries.</p><p>SOURCE: Archive of the Untamed. DATA: situated knowledge / informal ecologies / collective use / relations of care.</p><p>QUESTION: Can independent interfaces support intersectional struggles and collective spatial practice?</p></div></section>
  <section id="untamed" class="hyper-section hyper-previous"><span class="hyper-index">02 / PREVIOUS</span><div><h2>Archive → conflict → <em>observatory.</em></h2><p>RESEARCH LINEAGE / 05 STATES</p><div class="hyper-genealogy"><div class="hyper-genealogy-item"><span>01 / ARCHIVE OF THE UNTAMED</span><div><h3>Urban wildness / collective memory</h3><p>Participatory archive. Urban ecologies / situated media / informal spatial practices.</p></div></div><div class="hyper-genealogy-item"><span>02 / EVICTION AND SUBTRACTION</span><div><h3>Access revoked</h3><p>Eviction / restriction / enclosure. Record the process, not only the loss.</p></div></div><div class="hyper-genealogy-item"><span>03 / DECLARATIONS OF INTENT</span><div><h3>Institutional protocol</h3><p>RESTORE LEGALITY / ACCELERATE INTERVENTION. Analyse language, authority, urgency, spatial effects.</p></div></div><div class="hyper-genealogy-item"><span>04 / TOWARDS AN OBSERVATORY</span><div><h3>Distributed observation</h3><p>PROPOSED: independent observatory. NODES: archivists / documentarians / artists / explorers. PROTOCOL: collect / cross-reference / share.</p></div></div><div class="hyper-genealogy-item"><span>05 / A NETWORKED MEDIA ARCHIVE</span><div><h3>Shared media infrastructure</h3><p>TOPICS: occupation / artistic reappropriation / contested sites / public–private debounding / intersectional struggle. MEDIA: testimony / maps / images / sound / interfaces.</p></div></div></div><p class="hyper-pink-note">★ NOT ONLY WHAT DISAPPEARS. HOW ACCESS IS REMOVED.</p><div class="hyper-previous-links"><a href="https://thearchiveoftheuntamed.xyz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>01 / PREVIOUS RESEARCH</span>ARCHIVE OF THE UNTAMED ↗</a><span class="hyper-pending-link"><span>02 / PREVIOUS RESEARCH</span>ARCHIVE IS ALIVE <small>URL TO BE ADDED</small></span></div></div></section>
  <section id="system" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">03 / DIGITAL INFRASTRUCTURE</span><div><h2>Independent systems / <em>allied technologies.</em></h2><p>INTERFACE ≠ NEUTRAL. CONTROL: hosting / access / taxonomy / maintenance / circulation. TEST: independent platforms; collective governance; revisable relations.</p><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 01 — NETWORK / NON-HIERARCHICAL CONNECTIONS</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 900 380" role="img" aria-label="Rhizomatic archive network"><g class="wires"><path d="M450 184Q250 20 154 100M450 184Q680 12 758 92M450 184Q730 340 768 290M450 184Q210 365 145 292M154 100Q440 10 758 92M145 292Q460 330 768 290M154 100Q90 200 145 292M758 92Q850 180 768 290"/></g><g class="nodes"><circle cx="450" cy="184" r="51"/><circle cx="154" cy="100" r="35"/><circle cx="758" cy="92" r="35"/><circle cx="145" cy="292" r="35"/><circle cx="768" cy="290" r="35"/></g><g text-anchor="middle"><text x="450" y="169">HYPER</text><text x="450" y="181">ARCHIVE</text><text x="154" y="104">MEMORY</text><text x="758" y="96">ECOLOGIES</text><text x="145" y="296">SITES</text><text x="768" y="294">COMMUNITIES</text></g></svg></figure><p class="hyper-pink-note">★ ALLY OR CONTROL SYSTEM?</p><p>ALLIED TECHNOLOGIES = tools shaped with their users. DESIGN / MAINTAIN / REVISE / SHARE.</p><small>MODEL: relational / non-hierarchical / revisable.</small></div></section>
  <section id="space" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">04 / SPATIAL TRANSLATION</span><div><h2>Deploy / <em>public space.</em></h2><p>BOUNDARIES: public/private; physical/digital; archive/intervention. OUTPUT: spatial interfaces. METHODS: mapping / reversible structures / collective construction.</p><div class="hyper-columns"><div><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 02 — PROJECTION MAPPING</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 420 300" role="img" aria-label="Projection mapping onto a facade"><g class="wires"><path d="M85 72H315V258H85ZM112 98H176V154H112ZM220 98H283V154H220ZM112 180H176V236H112ZM220 180H283V236H220Z"/></g><g class="accent-wires"><path d="M30 265L112 98L283 154L390 265M30 265L112 236L283 98L390 265"/></g><text x="17" y="285">PROJECTOR</text></svg></figure><h3>01 / Projection mapping</h3><p>INPUT: archive fragments / maps / audiovisual records. OUTPUT: temporary urban projection.</p></div><div><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 03 — PARASITIC ARCHITECTURE</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 420 300" role="img" aria-label="Temporary reversible architecture"><g class="wires"><path d="M35 55H170V265H35ZM60 80H145V160H60ZM0 265H420"/></g><g class="accent-wires"><path d="M170 120L250 85L360 135L280 170ZM170 120V225L280 275V170M280 275L360 230V135M250 85V195L360 230M170 225L250 195L280 275"/></g><text x="195" y="57">REVERSIBLE</text><text x="195" y="70">ATTACHMENT</text></svg></figure><h3>02 / Parasitic architectures</h3><p>REVERSIBLE / SITE-RESPONSIVE / COLLECTIVELY ASSEMBLED.</p></div></div><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 04 — RECIPROCAL FEEDBACK / CURVED PATHS</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 900 260" role="img" aria-label="Curved reciprocal loop connecting archive, public interventions and new contributions"><g class="accent-wires"><path d="M180 130C280 12 370 12 450 130S640 248 730 130"/><path d="M730 130C650 8 555 8 450 130S280 252 180 130" stroke-dasharray="5 8"/><circle cx="180" cy="130" r="48"/><circle cx="450" cy="130" r="48"/><circle cx="730" cy="130" r="48"/></g><g text-anchor="middle"><text x="180" y="125">CRITICAL</text><text x="180" y="139">MAPPING</text><text x="450" y="125">DIGITAL</text><text x="450" y="139">AUTONOMY</text><text x="730" y="125">PUBLIC</text><text x="730" y="139">SPACE</text><text x="450" y="27">NEW TRACES / RETURN / REASSEMBLY</text></g></svg></figure></div></section>
  <section id="loop" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">05 / THE LOOP</span><div><h2>Map → host → <em>return → repeat.</em></h2><p>INPUT → ARCHIVE → INTERFACE → PUBLIC ACTION → NEW INPUT. ITERATE. No final state.</p><div class="hyper-loop" aria-label="Critical mapping loop"><div class="hyper-loop-step"><span>01 ★ MAP THE SUBTRACTED</span><p>Detect exclusion / erasure / surviving relations.</p></div><div class="hyper-loop-arrow">↓</div><div class="hyper-loop-step"><span>02 ★ RECLAIM THE DIGITAL</span><p>Independent hosting / shared protocols / revisable access.</p></div><div class="hyper-loop-arrow">↓</div><div class="hyper-loop-step"><span>03 ★ RETURN TO PUBLIC SPACE</span><p>Projection / parasitic structures / situated encounters.</p></div><div class="hyper-loop-return">↖ NEW TRACES / NEW CONFLICTS / MAP AGAIN ★</div></div></div></section>
  <section id="process" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">06 / TWO-MONTH RESIDENCY</span><div><h2>Research / <em>prototype / deploy.</em></h2><div class="hyper-steps"><p><strong>W01–02</strong>Fieldwork / collaborators / archive audit.</p><p><strong>W03–04</strong>Interface / critical mapping / spatial sketches.</p><p><strong>W05–06</strong>Build / fabricate / project / integrate.</p><p><strong>W07–08</strong>Field test / revise / document / share.</p></div><div class="hyper-columns"><div><h3>Artist contribution</h3><p>Web / code / audiovisual / mapping / laptop.</p></div><div><h3>Host / local collaboration</h3><p>Fabrication / projector / AV / local access / permits.</p></div></div><small>TARGET: working archive iteration + site-responsive installation. FORMAT: context-dependent.</small></div></section>
  <section id="references" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">07 / SELECTED REFERENCES</span><div><h2>Reference / <em>index.</em></h2><ol><li>Gilles Deleuze & Félix Guattari, <em>A Thousand Plateaus: Capitalism and Schizophrenia</em> (1980; English translation 1987). — Rhizomatic thinking.</li><li>Donna J. Haraway, <em>Staying with the Trouble: Making Kin in the Chthulucene</em> (2016). — Situated relationships and more-than-human worlds.</li><li>Stefano Harney & Fred Moten, <em>The Undercommons: Fugitive Planning & Black Study</em> (2013). — Collective study and self-organisation.</li><li>Stavros Stavrides, <em>Common Space: The City as Commons</em> (2016). — Commoning and shared urban space.</li><li>Shannon Mattern, <em>A City Is Not a Computer: Other Urban Intelligences</em> (2021). — Critical approaches to urban data and infrastructure.</li></ol><small>Research background: <a href="https://thearchiveoftheuntamed.xyz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Archive of the Untamed</a>.</small></div></section>
  <footer class="hyper-footer"><span>OTHERWISE HYPERARCHIVE / WORKING PROPOSAL / 2027</span><a href="#top">BACK TO TOP ↑</a></footer>
</article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.hyperarchive{--hyper-line:var(--line,#555);--hyper-accent:var(--signal,#ff71c3);width:100%;font:12px/1.65 "Courier New",monospace;color:var(--fg)}
.hyperarchive *{box-sizing:border-box}.hyperarchive a{color:inherit}.hyper-top,.hyper-footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hyper-line);font-size:10px}.hyper-hero{padding:70px 0 55px;min-height:52vh;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hyper-line)}.hyper-hero>span,.hyper-hero small,.hyper-index,.hyper-diagram figcaption,.hyperarchive small{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.07em;opacity:.75}.hyper-hero h1{font:400 clamp(34px,6.3vw,110px)/.96 "Courier New",monospace;letter-spacing:-.075em;margin:35px 0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.hyper-accent{color:var(--hyper-accent)}.hyper-hero p{font-size:clamp(13px,1.4vw,17px)}.hyper-nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px;padding:16px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hyper-line)}.hyper-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(130px,24%) minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px;padding:34px 0 48px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hyper-line)}.hyper-section>div{max-width:1000px}.hyper-section h2{font:400 clamp(18px,2.2vw,30px)/1.2 "Courier New",monospace;margin:0 0 24px}.hyper-section h3{font:400 12px "Courier New",monospace;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 12px}.hyper-section p{font:inherit;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 15px}.hyper-columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.hyper-diagram{position:relative;border:1px solid var(--hyper-line);margin:22px 0;overflow:hidden;padding:28px 6px 6px}.hyper-diagram figcaption{position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px}.hyper-diagram svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;min-height:160px}.hyper-diagram svg text{fill:var(--fg);font:10px "Courier New",monospace}.hyper-diagram .wires{stroke:var(--fg);opacity:.5;stroke-dasharray:3 7;fill:none}.hyper-diagram .nodes{stroke:var(--hyper-accent);fill:var(--bg);stroke-width:1.2}.hyper-diagram .accent-wires{fill:none;stroke:var(--hyper-accent);stroke-width:1.5}.hyper-steps{margin:30px 0}.hyper-steps p{display:grid;grid-template-columns:75px 1fr;gap:10px;border-top:1px solid var(--hyper-line);padding:12px 0;margin:0}.hyper-steps strong{color:var(--hyper-accent);font-weight:400}.hyper-section ol{padding-left:20px}.hyper-section li{margin:0 0 10px}.hyper-footer{border:0;margin-top:30px}.hyperarchive :target{scroll-margin-top:24px}
html[data-portfolio-mode="institutional"] .hyperarchive{--hyper-accent:#222;--hyper-line:#aaa}
@media(max-width:760px){.hyper-section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:15px}.hyper-columns{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hyper-hero{min-height:40vh;padding:40px 0}.hyper-top,.hyper-footer{flex-direction:column}}

.hyper-hero{position:relative;isolation:isolate;overflow:hidden}.hyper-hero>span,.hyper-hero>h1,.hyper-hero>p,.hyper-hero>small{position:relative;z-index:1}.hyper-hero-stars{position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;z-index:0}.hyper-hero-stars span{position:absolute;font:clamp(16px,3vw,42px)/1 monospace;color:var(--hyper-accent);opacity:.65;animation:hyper-twinkle 4s ease-in-out infinite alternate}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(1){left:8%;top:18%;animation-delay:-.3s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(2){left:84%;top:12%;animation-delay:-2s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(3){left:69%;top:44%;animation-delay:-1s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(4){left:94%;top:68%;animation-delay:-3s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(5){left:35%;top:8%;animation-delay:-2.6s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(6){left:55%;top:82%;animation-delay:-1.5s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(7){left:14%;top:76%;animation-delay:-.8s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(8){left:75%;top:90%;animation-delay:-3.3s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(9){left:96%;top:29%;animation-delay:-1.8s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(10){left:44%;top:54%;animation-delay:-2.8s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(11){left:3%;top:49%;animation-delay:-.9s}.hyper-hero-stars span:nth-child(12){left:61%;top:14%;animation-delay:-3.6s}@keyframes hyper-twinkle{0%{transform:scale(.65) rotate(-12deg);opacity:.2}100%{transform:scale(1.35) rotate(18deg);opacity:.9}}
.hyper-loop{border:1px solid var(--hyper-line);padding:clamp(16px,3vw,36px);margin-top:24px}.hyper-loop-step{border-top:1px solid var(--hyper-line);padding:16px 0}.hyper-loop-step span{font-size:clamp(13px,2vw,22px);color:var(--hyper-accent)}.hyper-loop-step p{margin:8px 0 0}.hyper-loop-arrow{font-size:28px;color:var(--hyper-accent);text-align:center}.hyper-loop-return{border-top:1px dashed var(--hyper-accent);padding:18px 0 0;color:var(--hyper-accent);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.05em}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.hyper-hero-stars span{animation:none!important}}

/* A little pink handwriting-like interruption to the otherwise austere mono layout. */
.hyperarchive{--hyper-pink:#ff78bd;--hyper-green:#b6ff00}
.hyper-section h2 em,.hyper-untamed p em{font-family:Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif!important;font-style:italic!important;font-weight:400;color:var(--hyper-pink);letter-spacing:-.025em}
.hyper-pink-note{font-family:Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif!important;font-size:clamp(18px,2.2vw,27px)!important;font-style:italic!important;color:var(--hyper-pink);max-width:640px}
.hyper-external{display:inline-block;border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;margin-top:12px;text-decoration:none}
.hyperarchive .hyper-diagram .accent-wires path{stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}
.hyperarchive .hyper-loop{border-radius:48% 8% 35% 6%/5% 30% 6% 20%;overflow:hidden}
.hyperarchive .hyper-loop-step{border-radius:60% 0 0 0/12% 0 0 0}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){.hyper-bitmap-fallback{animation:hyper-bitmap-drift 7s ease-in-out infinite alternate}@keyframes hyper-bitmap-drift{to{transform:translate(8px,-9px) rotate(5deg)}}}

/* Previous research: text-first, restrained, with no photographic effects. */
.hyper-previous-links{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:32px}
.hyper-previous-links>a,.hyper-pending-link{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;min-height:115px;padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--hyper-line);font:400 clamp(12px,1.6vw,17px)/1.3 "Courier New",monospace;text-decoration:none}
.hyper-previous-links>a:hover{border-color:var(--hyper-accent);color:var(--hyper-accent)}
.hyper-previous-links :is(a,.hyper-pending-link)>span{font-size:10px;opacity:.65}
.hyper-pending-link{opacity:.6}
.hyper-pending-link small{font-size:9px}
@media(max-width:600px){.hyper-previous-links{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
.hyper-genealogy{margin:30px 0}.hyper-genealogy-item{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(145px,28%) 1fr;gap:20px;padding:22px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--hyper-line)}.hyper-genealogy-item>span{font:11px/1.4 "Courier New",monospace;color:var(--hyper-accent)}.hyper-genealogy-item h3{font-size:clamp(15px,1.6vw,20px);text-transform:none;margin-bottom:10px}.hyper-genealogy-item p{margin-bottom:0}.hyper-genealogy-item:nth-child(even){padding-left:clamp(0px,2vw,20px)}@media(max-width:640px){.hyper-genealogy-item{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:9px}.hyper-genealogy-item:nth-child(even){padding-left:0}}
.hyperarchive .hyper-diagram .wires{stroke-width:.55!important;opacity:.42}.hyperarchive .hyper-diagram .nodes{stroke-width:.65!important}.hyperarchive .hyper-diagram .accent-wires{stroke-width:.65!important}.hyperarchive .hyper-diagram .accent-wires path,.hyperarchive .hyper-diagram .accent-wires circle,.hyperarchive .hyper-diagram .accent-wires rect{stroke-width:.65!important}.hyperarchive .hyper-section p{line-height:1.65}.hyperarchive .hyper-genealogy-item p{max-width:570px}
</style>

